    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Thank you\r\nEric, I am treating group size as a numeric variable. So, I hope it won&#39;t be a problem.  </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">According to your explanation, this model is an MCDS model with the region and the group size as\r\ncovariates:</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Hn08_null690_site&lt;-ds\r\n(sep08, key=&quot;hn&quot;, truncation=690, adjustment = NULL, formula = ~size\r\n+ as.factor(Region.Label), convert.units = 0.001)  <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I am having\r\nsome other doubts because I have tested this other model:  <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Hn08_null690&lt;-ds\r\n(sep08, key=&quot;hn&quot;, truncation=690, adjustment = NULL, formula = ~size,\r\nconvert.units = 0.001)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">But I am\r\nnot sure if this second model (Hn08_null690) might be a case of a CDS with\r\nstratification or an MCDS with without tacking in account strata. If the first case is correct, how can\r\nI write a CDS with stratification? I am doing these questions because I have\r\nsome surveys with a small sample size per stratum so, I am following the solutions\r\nindicated in Buckland et al. 2015 in sections 2.3.1 and 2.3. But I would like to\r\nbe sure that I am doing well with the codes. <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Also, for another\r\nsurvey I have tested the models below and I have obtained this data<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpaddi